    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In May 2026's seasonal heat, a generator failure at Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 acted like a comical slip of the machine, forcing the grid operator to raise a frantic red flag over the Visayas. To stop the grid from melting, officials then orchestrated a dramatic blackout ballet, ordering load shedding to protect the 230-kilovolt line. The outcome? A glorious blackout spectacle, with more than 950 megawatts vanishing from the grid.",
